+/**
+ * Bind a platform image (iOS/macOS: CVPixelBufferRef, Android: EGLImageKHR) as
+ * this texture's contents.
+ *
+ * Calls filament::Texture::setExternalImage(Engine&, void*) -- the overload
+ * marked UTILS_DEPRECATED at Texture.h:459-462 -- and does so deliberately.
+ * The non-deprecated ExternalImageHandleRef overload (Texture.h:435) requires
+ * Platform::createExternalImage(), which the Metal backend does not implement:
+ * MetalDriver::setupExternalImage2 is an empty body whose only content is
+ * "// FIXME: implement setupExternalImage2" (MetalDriver.mm:1250-1252).
+ * So on Metal the deprecated overload is currently the only one that works.
+ * Texture.h:447-448 documents its accepted types as "eglImageOES on Android
+ * and CVPixelBufferRef on iOS".
+ *
+ * PRECONDITION: the texture must have been built external, i.e. with
+ * Texture::Builder().sampler(SAMPLER_EXTERNAL) or .external(). Filament checks
+ * this with FILAMENT_CHECK_PRECONDITION(mExternal) (details/Texture.cpp:493),
+ * which aborts rather than returning an error. Note this constrains the
+ * TEXTURE, not the material: declaring the material parameter as `sampler2d`
+ * rather than `samplerExternal` is correct and is what Google's own AR sample
+ * does (ios/samples/hello-ar/Materials/camera_feed.mat), because on Metal the
+ * external image becomes an ordinary MTLTexture (MetalHandles.mm:700-707).
+ *
+ * OWNERSHIP: Filament takes its own reference; it does NOT adopt the caller's.
+ * setExternalImage begins with api.setupExternalImage(image), described at
+ * details/Texture.cpp:495-496 as "synchronous, and allows the driver to take
+ * ownership of the external image on this thread". On Metal that is a single
+ * CVPixelBufferRetain (MetalDriver.mm:1254-1262), documented there as
+ * "allowing the application to free their reference to the buffer"; the
+ * matching release is MetalDriver.mm:545. A caller holding a +1 must therefore
+ * release it after this call returns, and may safely do so immediately.
+ *
+ * Metal accepts only kCVPixelFormatType_32BGRA and
+ * kCVPixelFormatType_420YpCbCr8BiPlanarFullRange; any other format is a fatal
+ * check inside the backend, not a fallback. 420f additionally runs a
+ * ycbcr-to-rgb compute pass into a new RGB texture, so only 32BGRA is
+ * zero-copy.
+ */
